        "pull_request": {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ReactiveX/RxPY/pulls/845",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/ReactiveX/RxPY/pull/845",
          "diff_url": "https://github.com/ReactiveX/RxPY/pull/845.diff",
          "patch_url": "https://github.com/ReactiveX/RxPY/pull/845.patch",
          "merged_at": null
        },
        "body": "## Problem\n\n`delay_with_mapper` releases a source value from both the duration's `on_next` and `on_completed` callbacks. With a synchronous duration, its subscription has not yet been assigned when the first signal disposes it. Subsequent signals can therefore duplicate the source value or forward an error after the delay has already elapsed.\n\nFor example, an immediate duration created with `from_iterable([0], scheduler=ImmediateScheduler())` releases each source value twice.\n\n## Change\n\nApply `take(1)` to each duration and release the buffered value from its completion callback. Both an initial value and an empty completion release once; later values and errors are ignored after release. Scheduler forwarding and the public API are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nOn CPython 3.12.14:\n- Pristine upstream baseline: 1,580 passed, 15 skipped; all four configured pre-commit hooks passed.\n- New tests against original production: three failed; the empty-duration compatibility case passed.\n- Final full suite: 1,584 passed, 15 unchanged skips.\n- Ruff check/format, Pyright, Mypy, commit diff whitespace checks, and `uv build --no-sources` passed.\n- Independent review reran the full suite (1,584 passed, 15 skipped) and eight additional adversarial cases.\n\nRegression coverage includes a synchronous value followed by completion, several synchronous duration values, an empty duration, an error after release, and a None source value. Other Python/platform matrix combinations were not run locally.\n\nImplementation and independent review were AI-assisted. No human pre-review is claimed.",
